urnament","declaration_lines":[283,307],"file":"lean/QuarticQuery/Paper/QuantumTournamentFacts.lean","hypotheses":[],"inspection":{"axioms":["Classical.choice","Quot.sound","propext"],"module":"QuarticQuery.Paper.QuantumTournamentFacts","receipt":"corpus/reading_statement_evidence.json","status":"current","type":"∀ {ι Col : Type} [inst : Fintype ι] [inst_1 : Inhabited ι] [inst_2 : Fintype Col] [inst_3 : DecidableEq Col] {cc : ℕ}\n  {a : QuarticQuery.BitInput ι → Col → Col → ℝ},\n  2 ≤ Fintype.card Col →\n    (∀ (x : QuarticQuery.BitInput ι), QuarticQuery.Tournament.IsComparison (a x)) →\n      (∀ (i p : Col), QuarticQuery.Upper.Samples cc fun x b => QuarticQuery.Upper.bern (a x i p) b) →\n        have m := Fintype.card Col;\n        have T := QuarticQuery.Tournament.Tval m;\n        have ε := QuarticQuery.Tournament.epsval m;\n        ∃ C law,\n          ↑C ≤ 6072 * ↑cc * √↑m * ↑T ^ 2 * Real.log ↑T ∧\n            QuarticQuery.Upper.Samples (T * QuarticQuery.Paper.quantumStageReads m T cc ε) law ∧\n              QuarticQuery.Upper.Runs C law ∧\n                (∀ (x : QuarticQuery.BitInput ι) (o : QuarticQuery.Paper.QuantumCandidateList Col T), 0 ≤ law x o) ∧\n                  (∀ (x : QuarticQuery.BitInput ι), ∑ o, law x o = 1) ∧\n                    ∀ (x : QuarticQuery.BitInput ι) (s : Col),\n                      QuarticQuery.Tournament.Dominant (a x) ε s →\n                        1 - 2 * ↑m / 2 ^ T - ↑T * ε ≤ ∑ o, if s ∈ ↑o then law x o else 0"},"kind":"theorem","line":287,"note":"One bounded-list law with logical Samples witness, physical Runs witness, normalization, candidate inclusion inequality and explicit 6072 cap; law and budget are chosen before input and dominant candidate.","open_assumptions":[],"premises":["At least two candidates, comparison laws satisfying IsComparison and uniform coherent Samples cap."],"reached":false,"relation":"stronger","review_binding":{"declaration":"QuarticQuery.Paper.quantumTournament","judgment_sha256":"a709c2b872e6ebc06472c49ecd74a99f9c6bf08ea028c8d43891e1bb35c58813","row_sha256":"e19d6b5d3c220b2990cab3e950e027a5fd79f19e131c66109e58fcc50fab9b77","schema":"quartic-tie-review-v1","source_snapshot_sha256":"0d109ea9e9b7f4a766640d406409e30589fb4c5a4e645b6d6888569fa2edf29f","statement_id":"prop-3.2","statement_sha256":"214b204564641c704b973c7c3010a24e4b84d08a314a82a5fc0e8d2d3ed2820a"},"review_evidence":"current","reviewed_by":"ai:round3-construction-source-review","reviewed_relation":"stronger","reviewed_route":"same","route":"same","wrapper_comparison_evidence":"not_run"},{"build_evidence":"current","built":true,"compared":false,"comparison_credit":"none","comparison_evidence":"not_run","configured_checks":[],"declaration":"QuarticQuery.Paper.prop_3_2","declaration_lines":[181,310],"file":"lean/QuarticQuery/Paper/Section3.lean","hypotheses":[],"inspection":null,"kind":"theorem","line":194,"note":"","open_assumptions":[],"premises":[],"reached":false,"relation":"unassessed","review_evidence":"not_reviewed","reviewed_by":null,"reviewed_relation":"unassessed","reviewed_route":"unassessed","route":"unassessed","wrapper_comparison_evidence":"not_run"},{"build_evidence":"current","built":true,"compared":false,"comparison_credit":"none","comparison_evidence":"not_run","configured_checks":[],"declaration":"QuarticQuery.Tournament.ideal_tournament","declaration_lines":[334,360],"file":"lean/QuarticQuery/Tournament/Ideal.lean","hypotheses":[],"inspection":null,"kind":"theorem","line":338,"note":"Ideal process only: list length, miss probability 2m/2^T and the numerics. Upper.tournament_runs supplies the quantum algorithm, the query bound and the T eps sampling term.","open_assumptions":[],"premises":[],"reached":true,"relation":"unassessed","review_evidence":"legacy_unbound","reviewed_by":"ai:truth-auditor","reviewed_relation":"partial","reviewed_route":"same","route":"unassessed","wrapper_comparison_evidence":"not_run"},{"build_evidence":"current","built":true,"compared":false,"comparison_credit":"none","comparison_evidence":"not_run","configured_checks":[],"declaration":"QuarticQuery.Upper.tval_le","declaration_lines":[177,202],"file":"lean/QuarticQuery/Upper/Tournament.lean","hypotheses":["hv","hf","every v c <= eps"],"inspection":null,"kind":"theorem","line":178,"note":"Soundness of the list consumer: acceptance at most (length+T) eps. Section 3.3's union bound, not part of this row.","open_assumptions":["hv","hf","every v c <= eps"],"premises":[],"reached":true,"relation":"unassessed","review_evidence":"legacy_unbound","reviewed_by":"ai:truth-auditor","reviewed_relation":"partial","reviewed_route":"same","route":"unassessed","wrapper_comparison_evidence":"not_run"},{"build_evidence":"current","built":true,"compared":false,"comparison_credit":"none","comparison_evidence":"not_run","configured_checks":[],"declaration":"QuarticQuery.Upper.tournament_runs","declaration_lines":[362,492],"file":"lean/QuarticQuery/Upper/Tournament.lean","hypotheses":["2<=card Col","hc: IsComparison","hu: UnitValued","hcmp: comparison samplers of cc reads","hv: verifier programs of cV queries"],"inspection":null,"kind":"theorem","line":367,"note":"The quantum tournament, pointwise in x, on the bit oracle, with no order assumed. The list is not returned: it is consumed by the verifier v in continuation form, and the guarantee is 1-2m/2^T-T eps-eps <= acceptance when v s >= 1-eps. Taking v the indicator of s recovers list membership with one extra eps against the row. The total error in claim-error is unaffected.","open_assumptions":["2<=card Col","hc: IsComparison","hu: UnitValued","hcmp: comparison samplers of cc reads","hv: verifier programs of cV queries"],"premises":[],"reached":true,"relation":"unassessed","review_evidence":"legacy_unbound","reviewed_by":"ai:truth-auditor","reviewed_relation":"partial","reviewed_route":"same","route":"unassessed","wrapper_comparison_evidence":"not_run"}],"ledger_history":{"added_in_review":false,"adjudication_findings":[{"claim":"Drift identity, exact sampler and history-dependent coupling are sound.","id":"R1-AF-10","paper_locus":"Proposition 3.2, pp.8-9","reason":"Rederived each step, including W/m success and law w_i/W from Eq. 15, and the (1-f)ideal+f stop kernel with f<=eps. Script checks passed on finite instances.","verdict":"accepted"}],"earlier_ledger_wording":null,"wording_changed":false},"original_statement_sha256":"214b204564641c704b973c7c3010a24e4b84d08a314a82a5fc0e8d2d3ed2820a","passages":["CAT-prop-3.2"],"presentation":{"body":"Let $m\\ge2$, $T=\\lceil\\log_2(1000m)\\rceil$, $\\varepsilon=1/(1000T)$. For a coherent comparison circuit controlled by two candidate indices, reversible with all workspace retained, using at most $c\\ge1$ bit queries, with probabilities $a_{ij}$ satisfying equation (10), there is a quantum algorithm making $O(c\\sqrt m\\,T^2\\log T)$ queries on every branch and returning a list of at most $T$ candidates such that, for every fixed oracle input and every $i_*$ satisfying equation (11), the list contains $i_*$ with probability $\\ge1-2m/2^T-T\\varepsilon$.","body_plain":"Let m ≥ 2, T = ⌈log₂(1000m)⌉, ε = 1/(1000T). For a coherent comparison circuit controlled by two candidate indices, reversible with all workspace retained, using at most c ≥ 1 bit queries, with probabilities aᵢⱼ satisfying equation (10), there is a quantum algorithm making O(c√m T² log T) queries on every branch and returning a list of at most T candidates such that, for every fixed oracle input and every i★ satisfying equation (11), the list contains i★ with probability ≥ 1 − 2m/2ᵀ − Tε.","statement_sha256":"214b204564641c704b973c7c3010a24e4b84d08a314a82a5fc0e8d2d3ed2820a","title":"The quantum tournament lists a dominant candidate with high probability","title_plain":"The quantum tournament lists a dominant candidate with high probability"},"review_scope":{"compared_text":"maintained_ledger_statement","leading_matches":[{"declaration":"QuarticQuery.Paper.quantumTournament","file":"lean/QuarticQuery/Paper/QuantumTournamentFacts.lean"}],"relation_origin":"authored_review","semantic_examples":"none_indexed","type_and_axioms_origin":"compiled_lean_environment"},"section":"3.2","semantic_probes":[],"source_line":363,"statement":"Let m>=2, T=ceil(log_2(1000m)), epsilon=1/(1000T). For a coherent comparison circuit controlled by two candidate indices, reversible with all workspace retained, using at most c>=1 bit queries, with probabilities a_{ij} satisfying eq-10, there is a quantum algorithm making O(c sqrt(m) T^2 log T) queries on every branch and returning a list of at most T candidates such that, for every fixed oracle input and every i_* satisfying eq-11, the list contains i_* with probability >= 1-2m/2^T-T epsilon.","statement_sha256":"214b204564641c704b973c7c3010a24e4b84d08a314a82a5fc0e8d2d3ed2820a"}
